{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n\nsmiling-ancient-finwhale (2e85d8558a4) heals a reclaim-superseded clone on `append_event`, `transition_core` and `claim_core` (precheck raises `SupersededStoreRefused`; heal with the lock free; retry once). These still refuse such a clone until a read or idle-sync round moves it:\n\n- `rebar delete` (`_commands/delete.py::delete_cli`)\n- NDJSON import (`_io/import_ndjson.py::import_tickets`; `_flush` calls `_seam._refuse_unpublishable_store` directly)\n- a reconciler pass (`reconciler/inbound_translate.py::_write_event_file` → `finalize_event`)\n- claim or start work with the plan-review gate on: `gates.plan_review_precheck` and `claim --review`'s `claim._review_before_claim` call `claim_gate_check`, whose `freshness.store_freshness` reads a superseded clone as `diverged` and returns `stale-store`\n- a completion close when `sync.pull` is off: its only heal is `transition_close._refresh_close_material` → `ensure_fresh(force=True)`, which returns early under `sync.pull=off`, so the completion close gate refuses with `stale-store`.\n\n## Cause (reproduced)\n\nNone of these calls the heal. Reproduced at 2e85d8558a4 by `tests/interfaces/store/test_write_after_reclaim_other_paths.py`; per-path output is in the ticket comments. Not affected (tests pass there): a completion close with `sync.pull` on; review-plan with `sync.pull` on or off, because its repo snapshot (`_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py::_pin_tickets_sha`, `fetch=True`) calls `sync.reconverge` directly, not through `ensure_fresh`, before `_stale_store_verdict`.\n\n## Approach\n\n- **One heal entry.** `freshness.heal_superseded_clone(tracker, *, lock_timeout=...)` gains an optional lock budget (default unchanged). New `freshness.heal_if_superseded(tracker, repo_root) -> bool` probes `write_blocking_divergence` (local git only); only on a proven supersession it calls `heal_superseded_clone` with the read path's named short budget (`reads._RECONVERGE_LOCK_TIMEOUT`), re-probes, logs a WARNING naming the remote ref if the clone is still superseded, and returns whether it still is. Never raises.\n- **delete — heal-and-retry.** `delete_cli` holds no write lock and rolls back every file it wrote on `CommandError`. Move resolve-through-commit into one function wrapped in `_seam.retry_after_superseded_heal`; the rollback re-raises `SupersededStoreRefused`, so resolution and the child check are redone on the healed store.\n- **NDJSON import — heal before its reads.** `import_tickets` calls `heal_if_superseded` before `_scan_existing_source_ids`, so its id map, dedupe scan and buffered events are built on the healed store. A heal mid-run is not attempted: it could discard this import's own unpushed commits (the override replays nothing once the oldest unpushed event predates the reclaim horizon). Residual risk: a reclaim published while an import runs can still be fetched mid-run (pass-2e closes refresh and reconverge, and other processes share the tracker); `_flush`'s unchanged precheck then refuses the remaining chunks rather than strand them.\n- **reconciler pass — heal before, abort if unhealed.** A mid-pass heal is unsafe: by the first inbound write the pass has made outbound Jira mutations (so it cannot be retried) and holds uncommitted inbound event files and binding-state edits until `pass_support._commit_binding_store_snapshot`; the override's `reset --hard` would discard tracked edits. So `guarded_pass.run_pass_result` calls `heal_if_superseded` before `reconcile_once` (skipped for the read-only `preview` route) and, if the clone is still superseded, returns a RESCHEDULE result without calling `reconcile_once`, so no Jira mutation precedes a refused write.\n- **gated claim / start work — heal before the gate.** `gates.plan_review_precheck` and `claim._review_before_claim` call `heal_if_superseded` first. Both run before `claim_core`/`transition_core` take the lock, and `claim --review` no longer reads `stale-store` and pays for a needless review.\n- **completion close — heal in the pre-gate refresh.** `_refresh_close_material` (unforced closes only; before the open-child scan, state reduction and both close gates; outside the lock) also calls `heal_if_superseded`, independent of `sync.pull`. The verifier then reads the healed store and its receipt pins the healed tickets OID.\n- **Unchanged:** `store_freshness`, `claim_gate_check` and the read-only callers (`review-plan --status`, MCP `plan_review_status`, plan-review reuse) never run the heal; a `behind` store is still not adopted; review-plan; `completion_txn`, whose receipt check (`validate_receipt` → `non_ancestor_tickets_history`) makes retry-after-heal impossible by design.\n- `docs/concurrency.md`: extend the write-path heal paragraph with which writers heal-and-retry (append, transition, claim, delete), which heal before they start (import, reconciler pass, gated claim/start work, completion close) and why, that read-only gate queries never heal, and the import residual risk.\n- No new config key, env var or flag.\n\n## Scope\n\nIn: `src/rebar/_store/freshness.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/delete.py`, `src/rebar/_io/import_ndjson.py`, `src/rebar/reconciler/guarded_pass.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/gates.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/claim.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py`, `docs/concurrency.md`, `tests/interfaces/store/reclaim_harness.py` (shared fixture), `tests/interfaces/store/test_write_after_reclaim.py` (imports it), new `tests/interfaces/store/test_write_after_reclaim_other_paths.py`. Out: a clone whose remote ref has not been fetched yet.\n\n## Testing\n\nNew module, shared harness:\n- superseded clone: delete, import, reconciler pass, gated claim, gated start-work transition, and a `sync.pull=off` completion close (verifier stubbed) succeed on the reclaimed baseline (gated claim/start fail only for the missing attestation). Fail on 2e85d8558a4.\n- unrelated remote (lineage names another epoch): delete, import, reconciler pass, gated claim and the completion close gate are refused (DIVERGED; the gates via `stale-store` naming DIVERGED); clone, working tree and remote unchanged.\n- unchanged paths: `sync.pull=on` close and review-plan (both `sync.pull` values) reach their stubbed step healed; `claim_gate_check` on a superseded clone still reports `stale-store` and moves nothing.\n- heal failure: fetch failing, for comment, delete, import, reconciler pass, gated claim and `sync.pull=off` close; write lock held by another holder, for import, reconciler pass, gated claim and close (the short-budget sites). Each stays refused (the reconciler reschedules without calling `reconcile_once`); HEAD, working tree, an unpushed local event and the remote unchanged; no stale-override backup ref.\n\nExisting reclaim, gate-freshness, atomic-close, import and reconciler suites stay green, then `make verify`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] On a clone a reclaim superseded (remote lineage names the local epoch, remote ref already fetched), `rebar delete`, an NDJSON import and a reconciler pass each succeed and write on top of the reclaimed baseline; regression tests prove each and fail on 2e85d8558a4.\n- [ ] On such a clone the completion-close store-freshness gate and the plan-review claim gate move the clone and do not report `stale-store`; regression tests prove both and fail on 2e85d8558a4. The atomic completion commit itself is left unchanged for the receipt-ancestry reason recorded in the Approach.\n- [ ] Against a remote whose lineage does not name the local epoch, delete, import, the reconciler pass and the completion-close gate are still refused as DIVERGED and write nothing.\n- [ ] A heal that fails (failed fetch; write lock held by another holder) leaves the write refused as DIVERGED and loses no event: HEAD, the working tree, an unpushed local event and the remote are unchanged, and no stale-override backup ref is created.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1795256332663183001,"uuid":"6fc21839-7306-4788-acbf-c14c2554a41a"}